  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nThe ECMWF and GFS ensemble both suggest an upper trough will\nlinger over Manitoba through the next 7 days. This will not bring\nmuch for precipitation chances beside a brief passing shower in\nthe far north tonight. Wildfire smoke is expected to move in\nbriefly through the evening before exiting southeastward with the\ncold front that is currently moving through area. The HRRR goes\nout 48 hours and the RAP model goes about 51 hours at the maximum,\nso there is not a forecast for smoke just yet beyond two days into\nthe future. A Lake Wind Advisory is in effect for Fort Peck Lake \nand Red Flag Warning in effect south of the Missouri River this \nafternoon and evening.\n\nThe upper trough in Manitoba and shortwave troughs moving through\nthe overall flow are suggested by the ECMWF and GFS ensembles for\nSaturday night, and then again on Monday. There is some indication\nof this active pattern lingering past Monday to bring on and off\nchances for precipitation. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nThe only deviation was to increase winds with the cold front\nmoving through this afternoon.\n\nThere is high confidence in the Lake Wind Advisory today.\n\nThere is low confidence on precipitation occurring in the far\nnorth overnight.\n\nThere is moderate confidence of isolated smoke and haze reducing \nvisibility slightly around midday today.\n\nThere is high confidence in critical fire weather occurring \nthis afternoon south of the Missouri River.\n\nThere is low confidence on accumulating precipitation occurring\nthis weekend.",
